Q: Getting exception while trying to get controller_resolver intance in sonata crud controller A: <p>In Symony all services are private, so you must use Dependency Injection instead of retrieving instances directly from container.</p>
<p>Looking at following <a href="https://symfony.com/doc/current/create_framework/http_kernel_controller_resolver.html" rel="nofollow noreferrer">documentation</a>, it seems like you don't need to use DI at all:</p>
<pre><code>$controllerResolver = new HttpKernel\Controller\ControllerResolver();
$request = new Request([], [], ['_controller' =&gt; $controller]);
$exists = false !== $controllerResolver-&gt;getController($request);

</code></pre>
<hr />
<p>If you wish to dynamically change which controller will be executed, you can utilize <a href="https://symfony.com/doc/current/reference/events.html#kernel-controller" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>kernel.controller</code></a> Symfony event</p>
<pre><code>
use Symfony\Component\EventDispatcher\Attribute\AsEventListener;

#[AsEventListener(KernelEvents::CONTROLLER, 'onController')]
class Resolver
{
    public function onController(ControllerEvent $event): void
    {
        $controller = $event-&gt;getController();

        // ...

        $event-&gt;setController([$controller, $method]);
    }
}
</code></pre>

